# Generated, not authored. Asset catalogs are written by Xcode and a tool cache
# is rewritten on every run, so formatting them either fights a generator or
# produces a diff that reappears.
**/*.xcassets/
**/.impeccable/

# The same, for the native build. Gradle writes its CMake cache into the app's
# tree, and the app-level .gitignore covers that path, but prettier does not read
# .gitignore: without this line, anyone who has built Android locally fails the
# format check on files no one wrote.
**/android/app/.cxx/
